## 3. The AI Five-Layer Cake

### The Framework

Gerstner conceptualizes the AI value chain as a **five-layer cake**:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│        LAYER 5: APPLICATIONS         │  ← AVOID (mostly)
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│       LAYER 4: MODEL PROVIDERS       │  ← Selectively invest (OpenAI, Anthropic)
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│   LAYER 3: AI INFRASTRUCTURE (PaaS)  │  ← HEAVY — CoreWeave, cloud platforms
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│      LAYER 2: CHIPS / SILICON        │  ← HEAVY — Nvidia, Cerebras, AMD
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│        LAYER 1: ENERGY / POWER       │  ← HEAVY — nuclear, nat gas, grid infrastructure
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Layer-by-Layer Thesis

#### Layer 1: Energy

**Thesis:** AI inference consumes 10–100x the energy of traditional compute. Training a single GPT-4 class model consumes ~50–100 GWh. Inference at scale will demand gigawatt-scale data centers.

**Altimeter Positions:**
- Nuclear power exposure (via public equities)
- Natural gas infrastructure (backup/baseload for data centers)
- Grid equipment manufacturers (transformers, switchgear — 2–4 year lead times)

> *"The most important question in AI today is not 'can we build it?' — it's 'can we power it?' We will need 3-5x the current US electrical grid just for AI inference by 2030."* — Brad Gerstner

**Key Numbers:**
- Data center power demand: ~15 GW in 2023 → projected 80+ GW by 2030
- Transformer lead times: 18–24 months → 4–5 years currently
- Each 100MW data center requires ~$50-100M in grid interconnection infrastructure

#### Layer 2: Chips / Silicon

**Thesis:** Compute is the new oil. The chip layer captures the most value in the stack because it is the physical bottleneck. Nvidia has a 2–3 year lead, but alternatives (Cerebras, AMD) will capture share as inference dominates training spend.

**Altimeter Positions:**
- **Nvidia** — largest single position historically (8%+ of portfolio)
- **Cerebras** — private, wafer-scale bet (8–9 year research project)
- **AMD** — inference alternative as ROCm matures
- **Broadcom** — ASIC custom chip exposure (Google TPU, Meta, etc.)

> *"Nvidia is the most important company on earth right now. Period. They are the only company with a full-stack AI platform — hardware, software (CUDA), networking (Mellanox), and systems architecture."* — Brad Gerstner

#### Layer 3: AI Infrastructure (PaaS)

**Thesis:** Just as AWS became the dominant cloud layer of the last cycle, a new "AI-native" cloud is emerging. Hyperscalers (AWS, Azure, GCP) will coexist with AI-native providers.

**Altimeter Positions:**
- **CoreWeave** — AI-native cloud, purpose-built for GPU workloads. Started as a crypto mining operation, pivoted to AI.
- **AWS / Azure / GCP** — via public equities
- **Databricks** — data + AI platform layer (private position, massive conviction)

> *"CoreWeave is what AWS would have looked like if it was born in the AI era. Hyperscalers built for the mobile/cloud era. CoreWeave built for the GPU era."* — Brad Gerstner

#### Layer 4: Model Providers

**Thesis:** The model layer is essential but commoditizing. Open-source models (Llama, Mistral) compress margins. Winner-take-most dynamics favor the frontier model with the best distribution and capital access.

**Altimeter Positions:**
- **OpenAI** — private investment (led through Microsoft relationship)
- **Anthropic** — smaller position

> *"There's a $100B revenue opportunity in frontier models. But there's a $1T revenue opportunity in the infrastructure that runs them."* — Brad Gerstner

#### Layer 5: Applications — AVOID

**Thesis:** Most "AI applications" are thin wrappers around API calls with zero moat. The business logic that formerly lived in SaaS applications moves into the AI model layer. SaaS companies become "thin UI on top of a CRUD database" — easily replaced.

**Avoided or Underweight:**
- Most generative AI copywriting/design tools
- AI meeting note-takers
- AI customer support chatbots (generic)
- Single-feature AI plugs

> *"If you're building a thin UI on top of an API call to GPT-4, you don't have a business. You have a feature. And features don't compound. They get copied."* — Brad Gerstner

**Exception:** Companies in the "token flow" — data pipelines that feed AI models — these are durable.

