## 5. The 3-6-9 Heuristic

### The Framework

Gerstner's **3-6-9 heuristic** governs portfolio rebalancing based on market sentiment:

| Sentiment | Capital Deployment | Action |
|-----------|-------------------|--------|
| **30% (Euphoria)** | Trim positions | Reduce risk, raise cash |
| **60% (Equilibrium)** | Maintain | Hold, selective deploy |
| **90% (Despondency)** | Deploy heavily | Put capital to work |

### The Signal Metrics

- **30%**: When everyone is bullish, when cab drivers give stock tips, when your mother asks about crypto → trim
- **60%**: Normal markets, balanced sentiment, economic uncertainty priced in → maintain
- **90%**: When everyone is despondent, when funds are getting redemptions, when CEOs are panicking → deploy with maximum conviction

> *"The best time to deploy capital is when nobody wants to. The worst time is when everybody does. 3-6-9 keeps you disciplined."*

### Real-World Application: Nvidia Trim (2023)

In mid-2023, after Nvidia ran up 50%+ following the AI boom:

| Before Trim | After Trim |
|-------------|------------|
| 8% of portfolio | 6% of portfolio |
| Massive gains locked in | Room for upside |
| Rebalanced to other AI infra bets | Deployed into CoreWeave, Cerebras |

> *"We trimmed Nvidia from 8% to 6% after a 50% run-up. Not because we stopped believing. Because 3-6-9 tells us when the market has priced in too much optimism too fast."*

### Real-World Application: Jan 2023 (93% Net Long)

In January 2023 — the absolute trough of the tech bear market — Altimeter was:

- **93% net long** — maximum conviction deployment
- **Deploying dry powder** accumulated through the 2022 drawdown
- **Key buys**: Meta (Time to Get Fit thesis), Snowflake (oversold), Nvidia (<$150)

> *"January 2023 was a 9. Everyone was despondent. Crypto was dead. Tech was dead. 'AI is a bubble.' I've seen this movie before — it's the time to be greedy."*

### Mathematical Framework

Gerstner uses 3-6-9 as a **conviction-weighted position sizing** mechanism:

```
Position size = Base conviction × Sentiment factor

Where:
  Sentiment factor = 0.3 (trim) / 0.6 (maintain) / 0.9 (deploy)
  Base conviction = 0–100% based on 20-criteria rubric
```

