## 6. AI Infrastructure Bets

### Nvidia (Late 2022 Entry — Sub-$150)

**Entry Thesis:**
- Stock trading at ~30x P/E with earnings collapsing (crypto mining hangover + gaming slowdown)
- But: data center segment growing 100%+ YoY (hidden AI demand)
- Full-stack AI platform monopoly: hardware + CUDA + networking + systems

> *"In late 2022, Nvidia was a cyclical semiconductor stock trading at distressed multiples. The market was missing that it had become the AI infrastructure company. It was the cheapest AI company on earth because nobody was pricing the AI business correctly."*

**Key Metric:**
- Entry: ~$140–150 (split-adjusted ~$14–15)
- Peak (2024): >$1,000
- Position: 6-8% of portfolio
- Thesis: Nvidia is the "operating system of AI" — CUDA, not just chips

### Cerebras (8–9 Year Research Project)

**The Bet:**
Altimeter led/participated in multiple rounds. Cerebras builds **wafer-scale** chips — one monolithic chip the size of a dinner plate (vs. Nvidia's multi-die approach).

**Key Differentiators:**

| Dimension | Nvidia (H100/B200) | Cerebras (WSE-3) |
|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| **Die size** | ~814mm² (multi-die) | ~46,225mm² (single wafer) |
| **On-chip memory** | ~80GB HBM | ~44GB SRAM directly on wafer |
| **Inference speed** | Baseline | 15–18x faster for transformer models |
| **Memory bottleneck** | Off-chip HBM (main bottleneck) | SRAM adjacent to compute (no bottleneck) |

> *"Cerebras solved the memory wall problem that every other AI chip company is hitting. When you put SRAM directly next to every compute element, you eliminate the physical bottleneck of moving data. It's the only architectural solution I've seen that truly addresses the memory wall."*

**Memory Wall Problem (see Section 12):**
- Data movement consumes 100–1000x more energy than computation
- Von Neumann bottleneck: CPU/memory bus is the physical constraint
- Wafer-scale eliminates all off-chip data movement

**Altimeter Conviction:**
- 8–9 years of research before commercial viability
- First-mover in wafer-scale (no real competition)
- Inference advantage compounds as models get larger

### CoreWeave (AI-Native Neo-Cloud)

**The Thesis:**
CoreWeave started as a crypto GPU mining operation. In 2022, it pivoted entirely to AI inference/training cloud. Altimeter identified it as an "AI-native" cloud provider — purpose-built for GPU workloads.

**Advantage vs. Hyperscalers:**

| Dimension | Hyperscalers (AWS/Azure/GCP) | CoreWeave |
|-----------|------------------------------|-----------|
| **Network architecture** | General purpose | GPU-optimized InfiniBand |
| **GPU density** | 8–16 per rack | Up to 256 per rack |
| **Provisioning time** | Weeks | Hours |
| **Cost per GPU-hour** | Baseline | 30–40% cheaper |
| **Kubernetes-native** | Add-on | Core architecture |

> *"CoreWeave is the first cloud built for the GPU era, not the CPU era. They don't have 20 years of legacy infrastructure. They started from scratch for AI workloads. That's a massive advantage."*

**Altimeter Role:**
- Led/participated in multiple funding rounds
- Sat on board
- Helped structure "dribble lockup" IPO (see Section 11)

